stable-declaration-spacing

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Space adjacent let and const declarations by their formatted layout instead of their source layout, so a declaration that expands or collapses gets its blank line on the first pass and a second pass changes nothing.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream nufmt main spaces let and const groups by the formatted layout, so the first pass is stable for a declaration that expands or collapses.
